  "input": {
    "rationale": "Closing correction to the asserted snapshot-trigger defect so that one interpretation again covers the whole question with its current evidence. The claim itself is unchanged and still rests on its own witness (CheckRun 9cba2e79ff6c4019b0f0381690d9aaab: control false, then store_last=0 against snapshot_index=4 with commit and applied still 4 gives true). What changes is its reachability record: the follow-on execution (CheckRun b78bcab64b0d41b5adaafa98cc0c7f43) refuted the user-restore path as a second producer, because the Restore API's trailing noop leaves one entry above the snapshot index so store_last=105 against snapshot_index=104 keeps the delta small and the verdict false even after several intervals. Previously that producer was listed as predicted-but-untested; now it is a measured negative, and the snapshot-install path remains the only unexercised candidate. The bounded consequence (a redundant snapshot at the unchanged index, no safety effect) and the FSM-Snapshot prerequisite are retained unchanged.",
    "sources": [],
    "investigations": [],
